  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "In the 1900 date system, serial 0 is 1900-01-00 and serial 60 is the fictitious 1900-02-29",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527.20088 under the 1900 date system, serial 0 formats as 1900/1/0 (YEAR(0)=1900, MONTH(0)=1, DAY(0)=0), and 1900 is treated as a leap year so DATE(1900,2,29) returns 60, WEEKDAY(60,2) returns 3 (Wednesday), and DATE(1900,3,1)-DATE(1900,2,28) returns 2. EOMONTH(60,0) returns 59 (1900-02-28) rather than 60, whereas EDATE(60,12) returns 425 (1901-02-28).",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured on all 16 sheets (q001-q016) of fn5_dates_1900 in Excel 16.0.20527.20088.",
  "inferred": null,
  "documentation": null,
